// AUTO-GENERATED — do not hand-edit. Regenerate via the font
// rasterization script described below if the character set or font
// ever needs to change.
//
// Rasterized grayscale alpha masks for src/cctv/bitmapFont.js, produced
// by rendering the REAL Traditional Chinese font 'Noto Sans TC' (Regular,
// weight 400; via the npm package @fontsource/noto-sans-tc, OFL-1.1
// licensed) through a headless Chromium (Playwright) canvas at
// development/build time — never at Worker runtime. Only the resulting
// per-character alpha masks are committed here; the font file itself
// (@fontsource/noto-sans-tc, ~70MB of woff/woff2 across all Noto Sans TC
// weights/subsets) was installed in an isolated scratch directory purely
// as a rasterization input, was never added as a project dependency, was
// never committed, and is not shipped to Production in any form — this
// file's plain base64 alpha-mask strings are the only artifact that
// survives from that process. See PROJECT_HANDOFF.md's V1.8.3 section
// for the full pipeline, rationale, and the V1.8.3 hand-drawn-glyph
// attempt this replaced (found to be insufficiently legible on
// Production visual review).
//
// Format: each entry is { width, height, alphaBase64 } — alphaBase64
// decodes to exactly width*height bytes, one byte per pixel (0-255,
// row-major, top-to-bottom/left-to-right), representing how much of the
// glyph's fill color to blend in at that pixel (an alpha mask, not a
// full RGBA image — bitmapFont.js supplies the color at draw time).
// CJK glyphs are 32x32 ("full-width"); ASCII/digit/symbol glyphs are
// 16x32 ("half-width") — both share the same 32px row height so mixed
// CJK+ASCII text lines up on one baseline.

